      "argument": [
        {
          "id": "S001",
          "text": "By H007 every X_r,Y_r preserves M, so its restriction is a Z-linear endomorphism. Inclusion M→V is injective because M is a submodule. The original complex identities r!X_r=x^r and r!Y_r=y^r therefore restrict to r!X_M(r)=x_M^r and r!Y_M(r)=y_M^r for every r≥0. These are identities using integer multiples of operators, with no division in M. By H005, h=xy−yx, so h preserves M and restricts to h_M=x_M y_M−y_M x_M. The inclusions intertwine x_M,y_M,h_M with x,y,h.",
          "uses": [
            "H005",
            "H007"
          ],
          "uses_local": [],
          "objects": [
            "M",
            "V",
            "X",
            "Y",
            "X_M",
            "Y_M",
